    <string name="about_translations">About translations</string>
    <string name="about_title">Translation sources</string>
    <string name="about_intro">The Quran is the Arabic text. Translations convey its meanings and are the work of scholars; for deeper study, refer to the Arabic text and a qualified teacher.</string>
    <string name="about_arabic_title">Arabic text — Uthmani script</string>
    <string name="about_arabic_body">The standard Uthmani text as verified and published by the Tanzil Project (tanzil.net).</string>
    <string name="about_uz_title">Uzbek — Shaykh Muhammad Sodiq Muhammad Yusuf</string>
    <string name="about_uz_body">Translation of the meanings of the Quran by Shaykh Muhammad Sodiq Muhammad Yusuf (1952–2015), Mufti of the Spiritual Administration of Muslims of Central Asia and Kazakhstan (1989–1993) and author of the tafsir «Tafsiri Hilol». It is one of the most widely read Uzbek translations; the Committee on Religious Affairs under the Cabinet of Ministers of Uzbekistan announced its publication in Latin script.\n\nOriginal script: Cyrillic. The Latin version in this app is converted automatically letter by letter, so rare spelling differences are possible.\n\nNote: Uzbekistan has no single legally designated “official” translation. The translations by Alouddin Mansur (1992) and Abdulaziz Mansur (2001) are also recognized; they are not included in this version.</string>
    <string name="about_ru_title">Russian — Elmir Kuliev</string>
    <string name="about_ru_body">Translation of the meanings of the Quran by the Azerbaijani Islamic scholar Elmir Kuliev, completed in 2002 and revised in later editions; one of the most widely used Russian translations.</string>
    <string name="about_en_title">English — Saheeh International</string>
    <string name="about_en_body">Translation by three American Muslim women translators, published in 1997 by Abul-Qasim Publishing House, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia.</string>
    <string name="about_data_title">Data and fonts</string>
    <string name="about_data_body">The texts are taken from the open Al-Quran Cloud API (alquran.cloud) when the app is built and are stored inside the app; nothing is downloaded on your phone. Arabic fonts: Google Fonts, SIL Open Font License.</string>
